legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability only applies during the controller\u2019s next untap step, even if the permanent has been the target of Ojutai\u2019s triggered ability more than once. The permanent won\u2019t stay tapped through multiple untap steps.","oracle_id":"27d7f737-59a4-4948-9b2e-599ae848e054","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability tracks the permanent, but not its controller. If the permanent changes controllers before its first controller\u2019s next untap step, then it won\u2019t untap during its new controller\u2019s next untap step.","oracle_id":"27d7f737-59a4-4948-9b2e-599ae848e054","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The triggered ability can target a nonland permanent that\u2019s already tapped. That permanent won\u2019t untap during its controller\u2019s next untap step.","oracle_id":"27d7f737-59a4-4948-9b2e-599ae848e054","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature attacks alone if it's the only creature declared as an attacker during the declare attackers step. For example, Asari Captain's triggered ability won't trigger if you attack with multiple creatures and all but one of them are removed from combat.","oracle_id":"32e7385e-525e-4925-8cfd-bfea21fcd1bf","published_at":"2022-02-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Asari Captain's triggered ability gives the solitary attacker +1/+0 for each creature you control that is either a Samurai or a Warrior as it resolves, including the attacker itself, if applicable. A creature that is both a Samurai and a Warrior is only counted once.","oracle_id":"32e7385e-525e-4925-8cfd-bfea21fcd1bf","published_at":"2022-02-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Affected creatures lose all other colors and are mono-black.","oracle_id":"5667376e-e59c-4b17-b096-5d92cdfe3db1","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Bolster itself doesn\u2019t target any creature, though some spells and abilities that bolster may have other effects that target creatures. For example, you could put counters on a creature with protection from white with Abzan Skycaptain\u2019s bolster ability.","oracle_id":"73520b5a-3d55-40c9-af60-90fdd811934f","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each Dragon you attack with will cause Dromoka\u2019s triggered ability to trigger. For each instance of the ability, you\u2019ll determine which creature to put +1/+1 counters on as it resolves. Specifically, the creature you control with the lowest toughness as the first such ability resolves may not have the lowest toughness as the second such ability resolves.","oracle_id":"73520b5a-3d55-40c9-af60-90fdd811934f","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You determine which creature to put counters on as the spell or ability that instructs you to bolster resolves.","oracle_id":"73520b5a-3d55-40c9-af60-90fdd811934f","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect causes Dress Down to become a creature, it will lose its own abilities along with all other creatures. This includes the triggered ability that causes it to be sacrificed at the beginning of the end step.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect grants a creature an ability after Dress Down has entered the battlefield, it won't lose that ability. For example, if a land becomes a creature while Dress Down is on the battlefield, it will still gain any abilities given to it by the effect that animated it. It will, however, lose any abilities it already had.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won\u2019t return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura\u2019s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn\u2019t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent\u2019s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura\u2019s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can\u2019t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it\u2019s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners\u2019 graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8","published_at":"2020-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature that is equipped is considered modified no matter who controls the Equipment that's attached to it.","oracle_id":"ecfabd06-c059-4f3d-9e5f-587364033cac","published_at":"2022-02-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature with a counter on it is considered modified no matter what kind of counter it is or which player put it on that creature.","oracle_id":"ecfabd06-c059-4f3d-9e5f-587364033cac","published_at":"2022-02-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An Aura controlled by an opponent does not cause a creature you control to be modified.","oracle_id":"ecfabd06-c059-4f3d-9e5f-587364033cac","published_at":"2022-02-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must still pay all costs and follow all normal timing rules to play a card this way. For example, you may play a land this way only during your own main phase while the stack is empty, and only if you have not yet played a land this turn.","oracle_id":"ecfabd06-c059-4f3d-9e5f-587364033cac","published_at":"2022-02-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature enters the battlefield as a copy of or becomes a copy of a creature whose dash cost was paid, the copy won\u2019t have haste and won\u2019t be returned to its owner\u2019s hand.","oracle_id":"f6e160c1-b29f-4f3d-ab55-43ffe3ab4acf","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you choose to pay the dash cost rather than the mana cost, you\u2019re still casting the spell. It goes on the stack and can be responded to and countered. You can cast a creature spell for its dash cost only when you otherwise could cast that creature spell. Most of the time, this means during your main phase when the stack is empty.","oracle_id":"f6e160c1-b29f-4f3d-ab55-43ffe3ab4acf","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you pay the dash cost to cast a creature spell, that card will be returned to its owner\u2019s hand only if it\u2019s still on the battlefield when its triggered ability resolves. If it dies or goes to another zone before then, it will stay where it is.","oracle_id":"f6e160c1-b29f-4f3d-ab55-43ffe3ab4acf","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You don\u2019t have to attack with the creature with dash unless another ability says you do.","oracle_id":"f6e160c1-b29f-4f3d-ab55-43ffe3ab4acf","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any permanent can be targeted by the second ability, not just one with counters on it.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Vampire Hexmage's ability can't target a permanent card in a zone other than the battlefield, such as a suspended card.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
